<title>USA: K-tel postpones Platinum deal vote.</title>
<headline>K-tel postpones Platinum deal vote.</headline>
<dateline>PLYMOUTH, Minn. 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>K-tel International Inc said Wednesday it has postponed the special shareholder meeting scheduled for a vote on the sale of most of its worldwide music buiness to Platinum Entertainment Inc.</p>
<p>The new meeting date is August 19. The meeting was postponed from July 31 in order to meet regulatory requirements for the time between a Securities and Exchange Commission filing and the meeting date, the company said.</p>
<p>K-tel shares closed unchanged at 7-3/4 Wednesday.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
